@startuml
title Sequence diagram: organiser submits, Lead assigns a coordinator
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' Submitting saves the request as "submitted" with no coordinator; it writes no history
' entry. Assigning saves the coordinator and a history entry in one commit, and the two
' notifications after it. A notification is only a record in PostgreSQL: nothing is
' pushed to its recipient (no email, websocket or polling), who fetches it later with
' GET /api/notifications.

actor "Event\nOrganiser" as organiser
actor "Coordinator\nLead" as lead
actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Organiser submits an event request (their account must belong to a client organisation) ==
organiser -> web : Fill in the request
autonumber
web -> api : POST /api/events/requests
api -> db : Insert event request\n(submitted)
api -> db : Save notification:\nevery Coordinator Lead
api --> web : The new request: reference and status
autonumber stop
web --> organiser : Show the reference

== Later, the Web App fetches the Lead's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
lead -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : A new request is waiting in the queue
autonumber stop
web --> lead : Show notifications

== Lead opens the unassigned queue (Lead only) ==
lead -> web : Open the queue
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/events/requests/unassigned
api --> web : Requests waiting for a coordinator
autonumber stop
web --> lead : Show the queue

== Lead assigns a coordinator (the request must be waiting in the queue) ==
lead -> web : Assign a coordinator
autonumber resume
web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/\n:reference/coordinator
api -> db : Set the coordinator, add\na history entry
api -> db : Save notification: coordinator
api -> db : Save notification: organiser
api --> web : The request, with the coordinator's\nname and email
autonumber stop
web --> lead : Show the coordinator

== Later, the Web App fetches the coordinator's and organiser's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
coordinator -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : You have been assigned\nto coordinate an event
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show notifications

organiser -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : A coordinator has been\nassigned to your request
autonumber stop
web --> organiser : Show notifications
@enduml
